SQL Sales Analysis Project
This project demonstrates how to use SQL for data analysis with a sample sales dataset of 200 rows. The dataset contains information about customer orders, product categories, quantities, prices, and regions. It serves as a practical reference for learning and applying SQL queries.

📊 Dataset Overview
The dataset includes:

Order details: Order ID, Customer Name, Order Date

Product information: Category, Sub‑Category, Product Name

Sales metrics: Quantity, Unit Price, Total Price

Geography: Region of sale

🎯 Learning Objectives
Using this dataset, you can practice:

Basic queries: SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, GROUP BY

Aggregations: SUM, AVG, COUNT

Joins and Subqueries: Combining tables and filtering with nested queries

CASE statements: Applying conditional logic in queries

📝 Assignments
Find top customers by revenue

Calculate average order values

Analyze yearly sales trends

Explore category‑wise performance
